1. **A cell stack device comprising:**

a plurality of elongated cells arranged in a stacked configuration, each elongated cell extending along a longitudinal axis and comprising:

- a supporting substrate;
- a fuel electrode disposed over the supporting substrate;
- a solid electrolyte disposed over the fuel electrode;
- an air electrode disposed over the solid electrolyte; and
- an interlayer disposed between the solid electrolyte and the air electrode, the interlayer having a porosity greater than a porosity of the solid electrolyte; and

at least one electrical connector electrically connecting the plurality of elongated cells.
